Create a service account.

USAGE
  $ axway service-account create [--json] [--no-banner] [--no-color] [--profile <value>] [--desc <value>] [--name <value>] [--org <value>] [--public-key <value>] [--role <value>...] [--secret <value>] [--account <value>]

FLAGS
  --account=<value>     The account to use within the active profile.
  --desc=<value>        The description of the service account.
  --name=<value>        Friendly name to use for display.
  --org=<value>         The organization name, id, or guid; defaults to the current org.
  --public-key=<value>  The path to the public key.
  --role=<value>...     Assign one or more organization roles to the service account.
  --secret=<value>      A custom client secret key.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --json             Format output as json.
  --no-banner        Disable the banner.
  --no-color         Disable color output.
  --profile=<value>  Specify the configuration profile to use.

DESCRIPTION
  Create a service account.

  A service account requires a name and either a client secret key or a PEM formatted public key.

  The service account's client id is autogenerated by the platform based on the provided name.

  If the service account name is not specified, then the command will interactively prompt for all values. If prompting is not available, then all required options must be passed in at execution.

ALIASES
  $ axway service-account add
  $ axway service-account new

EXAMPLES
  Create a service account and prompt for name, type, etc

    $ axway service-account create

  Create a service account with a auto-generated client secret key

    $ axway service-account create --name foo

  Create a service account with a custom client secret key

    $ axway service-account create --name foo --secret bar

  Create a service account with a PEM formatted public key

    $ axway service-account create --name foo --public-key /path/to/public_key.pem

